{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And Jacob lifted his feet.</b> When a man walks of his own will toward a destination known to him, it is fitting to say that he lifts his feet. But when he departs from a place where there is no rest for the sole of his foot, it is fitting to say that his feet carry him, as in: יוֹבִילוּהָ רַגְלֶיהָ — 'her feet shall carry her' (Isaiah 23:7)."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:32:12.386198803Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}